# Copy to .env in the repository root for optional GitHub recollection.
# The final-analysis notebooks use downloaded data and need no token.
# See RECONSTRUCTION.md for commands, working directories, and prerequisites.
# Use tokens authorized to read the public repository metadata being collected.
# Do not commit credentials.
#
# The human-PR and check-run collectors accept a single token.
# rq3/get_yaml_diff_files.py reads GITHUB_TOKEN from the process environment;
# it does not load .env itself. RECONSTRUCTION.md shows how to load it.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# data_collection_scripts/fetch-ai-workflow-commits-meta.py requires at least
# FIVE DISTINCT VALID TOKENS in its current configuration. The other collectors
# also accept this comma-separated pool. Do not repeat one token five times.
# GITHUB_TOKENS=token_one,token_two,token_three,token_four,token_five
